\description{
Density, random generation, and \code{brms} custom family for a single-accumulator
Linear Ballistic Accumulator. Evidence rises linearly and ballistically - no
within-trial noise - from a start point drawn uniformly on \verb{[0, sigmabias]}
at a rate drawn from a normal truncated at zero, until it reaches the
threshold \code{b = sigmabias + boundary}. That finishing time is shifted by a
non-decision time \code{ndt}, and a fixed proportion \code{poutlier} of responses is
generated by an outlier process instead.

Fixing \code{sigmabias = 0} gives the \strong{recinormal}, or LATER, model, in which
\code{1 / (RT - ndt)} is normally distributed; see the section below.

Functions:
\itemize{
\item \code{rcogmod_lba1()}: Simulates random draws.
\item \code{dcogmod_lba1()}: Computes the density (likelihood).
\item \code{cogmod_lba1()}: Creates a \code{brms::custom_family()}.
\item \code{cogmod_lba1_stanvars()}: Generates the \code{stanvars} to pass to \code{brm()}.
}
